 ===== arc audit --help =====
 Record a review performed after integration (never a late verdict)
 
-An audit discharges a debt when its auditor is independent of the work's contributors. A debt of kind `ineligible-review` also needs routing's word that the auditor is eligible: `--assessment <file>` with `independence: eligible`. Without one, or with an `ineligible` assessment, the audit is recorded and listed beside the obligation, which stays open. The assessment must also describe the auditor that records the audit: the audit's recorded model, and its effort where both name one, must match the reviewer's `identities` and `effort`. Otherwise the audit is recorded, says why, and is listed beside the obligation, which stays open. Every other kind needs an independent read without a routing assessment.
+An audit discharges a debt when its auditor is independent of the work's ledger authorship: the patchset's declared contributors, else its effective author, and its production record's implementer. Planning and orchestrating never refuse; the audit records those roles beside the verdict. A debt of kind `ineligible-review` also needs routing's word that the auditor is eligible: `--assessment <file>` with `independence: eligible`. Without one, or with an `ineligible` assessment, the audit is recorded and listed beside the obligation, which stays open. The assessment must also describe the auditor that records the audit: the audit's recorded model, and its effort where both name one, must match the reviewer's `identities` and `effort`. Otherwise the audit is recorded, says why, and is listed beside the obligation, which stays open. Every other kind needs an independent read without a routing assessment.
 
 An `ineligible-review` debt is also cleared only when the assessment's authors answer to the model of every `Implemented-by` line in the audited range. An assessment that omits one is recorded with binding `authors-uncovered`, names the omitted models, and leaves the debt open. When the range's `Implemented-by` lines cannot be established (the production record kept none and the range does not read) the binding is `authors-unread` and the debt stays open too.
 
-An approving audit recorded under the model of an `Implemented-by` line in the audited range, at any effort, warns that it shows a review happened and not that it was independent of whoever wrote the work. Where `forbid_self_approval` is on it is refused, with the remedy a contributor match gets. Such a read never discharges review debt, regardless of self-approval policy: permission to approve does not establish independent coverage. `--verdict changes-requested` is open to anyone.
+An approving audit recorded under the model of the ledger's implementer of the audited range, at any effort, warns that it shows a review happened and not that it was independent of whoever wrote the work. Where the ledger records no implementer model, the audit says so and is judged by the actor, session and harness; `Implemented-by` trailers are reported as declared text only. A debt recorded before production summaries existed still reads the shipped patchset's ledger authorship, including a historical integrated closure that recorded only its integrated commit. Where `forbid_self_approval` is on it is refused, with the remedy a contributor match gets. Such a read never discharges review debt, regardless of self-approval policy: permission to approve does not establish independent coverage. `--verdict changes-requested` is open to anyone.
 
